      "writtenOn": "2021-03-06T02:02:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The mechanism is applied to wherever a link is made. So, yes, it applies to APEX-to-APEX linkages as well.\n\nBy the way, as we have discussed in the meeting, the mechanism uses the \"platform sdk version\" as the only marker. This means that, module A won\u0027t be able to call a new API defined in module B when running on an old platform, even when the module B is the up-to-date one having the new API.\n\nThis is what I called as \"conservative\". If calling the new API is really needed, module A could use dlopen/dlsym technique instead.",
      "parentUuid": "cef0908f_878dbda4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 52
      },
